(2668593, 362451, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>What an interesting shot.  I''m not a big fan of abstract, okay, scratch that, the truth is that I usually just don''t get it but I like this.  I like the patterns, the lines, the way light on the subject, natural is always the way to go, heh?<br/> <br/>What bothered me about it and I would have subtracted a point is the noise  or patterns that show up in the green areas.  I guess it all goes with the abstract idea but like I said, I never did get abstract, probably why I didn''t vote on it, LOL<br/> <br/>The only other thing I noticed was the upper left corner, that black area is a bit distracting.  Other than that it''s a wonderful shot and you did a great job!<br/> <br/>I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! What an interesting shot.  I''m not a big fan of abstract, okay, scratch that, the truth is that I usually just don''t get it but I like this.  I like the patterns, the lines, the way light on the subject, natural is always the way to go, heh? What bothered me about it and I would have subtracted a point is the noise  or patterns that show up in the green areas.  I guess it all goes with the abstract idea but like I said, I never did get abstract, probably why I didn''t vote on it, LOL The only other thing I noticed was the upper left corner, that black area is a bit distracting.  Other than that it''s a wonderful shot and you did a great job! I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges! Deannda', '2006-07-27 17:02:56.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2668657, 363693, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This photo is making me hungry!  LOL :) This is a late night snack?  I''m coming to visit at your house! :)<br/> <br/>A nice shot but that''s it, a nice shot.  As you can see from some of the other shots the idea was to offer a more abstract feel or setting to the shot.  This, with the proper PS treatment would make a wonderful ad for a turkey (is it turkey) sandwich.<br/> <br/>THe light is a bit harsh on the top and the shadows to the right are very distracting.   Maybe the use of a reflector of fill light to balance it out?<br/> <br/>This could have been more abstract to me, (but trust me when I say I''m the last person to ask about abstract art) is if you had arranged the celery and cherrie and did a more macro shot of them.  Maybe with the bread in part of it?<br/> <br/>I really like your shell shot in your profile, you''ve got a good eye overall.<br/> <br/>I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This photo is making me hungry!  LOL :) This is a late night snack?  I''m coming to visit at your house! :) A nice shot but that''s it, a nice shot.  As you can see from some of the other shots the idea was to offer a more abstract feel or setting to the shot.  This, with the proper PS treatment would make a wonderful ad for a turkey (is it turkey) sandwich. THe light is a bit harsh on the top and the shadows to the right are very distracting.   Maybe the use of a reflector of fill light to balance it out? This could have been more abstract to me, (but trust me when I say I''m the last person to ask about abstract art) is if you had arranged the celery and cherrie and did a more macro shot of them.  Maybe with the bread in part of it? I really like your shell shot in your profile, you''ve got a good eye overall. I hope my comments help and Good Luck in future Challenges! Deannda', '2006-07-27 17:12:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669591, 364424, 44751, '<td valign="top">Well done on 15th!  Superb shot.  Go Team Pentax!!!!!<br/> <br/>Nic.</td>', 'Well done on 15th!  Superb shot.  Go Team Pentax!!!!! Nic.', '2006-07-27 22:23:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669597, 364604, 44751, '<td valign="top">Well done to our fearless leader!  Very clever shot.  Go Team Pentax!!!<br/> <br/>Nic.</td>', 'Well done to our fearless leader!  Very clever shot.  Go Team Pentax!!! Nic.', '2006-07-27 22:25:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2669985, 364077, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>First off, welcome to DPC!  I really like to do critiques for younger members.  It''s really cool to see what one can do before they become brainwashed by how things are ''supposed'' to be done!<br/> <br/>OK, This is probably gonna be the hardest critique I''ve ever done.  You see I like to use this technique that I call "what I like/don''t like" and I still haven''t found anything that I truly like about this shot...<br/> <br/>Why doesn''t this shot work?  The focus is a little off.  You said youself that you didn''t use a tripod.  This and a slow shutter speed probably contributed to the focus problems.  Whenever you do a setup shot there is really no reason not to use a tripod.  My photography improved by leaps and bounds when I started to use a tripod religiously!  The colors as well as overall contrast are quite flat.  I can''t tell in this shot if you used the flash or if this was taken outdoors in bright sunlight.  On camera flash for a shot like this will basically wash out the tonality of the colors.  It (or the bright sun for that matter) can also cause blown out areas like the white in the center of the spiral.  It will also remove the depth of the shot.   A little sidelighting would probably have improved this considerably!<br/> <br/>The above are all technical reasons this shot didn''t do to well.  There are a bunch of compositional reasons also.  To make it simple, there''s just too damn much goin'' on.  Your eye has no where to rest.  I mean ya got some pretty cool lines.  The spiral is pretty cool.  The carrots are pretty cool.  The both lead toward the center of the shot but there''s nothing really there to see...  All the other stuff in the shot just seem like noise.  I don''t see why they''re there...<br/> <br/>Put all this together and you have a shot that doesn''t score well.  If you look at the top twenty shots of this challenge, you''ll see nice simple sharp shots.  That''s what does well here...<br/> <br/>Please don''t take any of this as mean.  I''m just tryin'' to help out a new member.  Please keep shootin'' and postin''!  I can''t wait to see what else ya got in your camera...<br/> <br/>Yours<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club: First off, welcome to DPC!  I really like to do critiques for younger members.  It''s really cool to see what one can do before they become brainwashed by how things are ''supposed'' to be done! OK, This is probably gonna be the hardest critique I''ve ever done.  You see I like to use this technique that I call "what I like/don''t like" and I still haven''t found anything that I truly like about this shot... Why doesn''t this shot work?  The focus is a little off.  You said youself that you didn''t use a tripod.  This and a slow shutter speed probably contributed to the focus problems.  Whenever you do a setup shot there is really no reason not to use a tripod.  My photography improved by leaps and bounds when I started to use a tripod religiously!  The colors as well as overall contrast are quite flat.  I can''t tell in this shot if you used the flash or if this was taken outdoors in bright sunlight.  On camera flash for a shot like this will basically wash out the tonality of the colors.  It (or the bright sun for that matter) can also cause blown out areas like the white in the center of the spiral.  It will also remove the depth of the shot.   A little sidelighting would probably have improved this considerably! The above are all technical reasons this shot didn''t do to well.  There are a bunch of compositional reasons also.  To make it simple, there''s just too damn much goin'' on.  Your eye has no where to rest.  I mean ya got some pretty cool lines.  The spiral is pretty cool.  The carrots are pretty cool.  The both lead toward the center of the shot but there''s nothing really there to see...  All the other stuff in the shot just seem like noise.  I don''t see why they''re there... Put all this together and you have a shot that doesn''t score well.  If you look at the top twenty shots of this challenge, you''ll see nice simple sharp shots.  That''s what does well here... Please don''t take any of this as mean.  I''m just tryin'' to help out a new member.  Please keep shootin'' and postin''!  I can''t wait to see what else ya got in your camera... YoursTC', '2006-07-28 00:33:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2670119, 363798, 22975, '<td valign="top">not a fan of the highlights, if that''s what that is in the yogurt.  composition''s good.</td>', 'not a fan of the highlights, if that''s what that is in the yogurt.  composition''s good.', '2006-07-28 01:23:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2670788, 363756, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh!  Should have known this came from an Aussie, since it''s upside down!  Well executed shot - the blue plate/bowl has a texture which works well to depict "water", and you did a very good job keeping the texture of the ice cream.  Hopefully, you got to eat the evidence after the picture was taken.</td>', 'Heh!  Should have known this came from an Aussie, since it''s upside down!  Well executed shot - the blue plate/bowl has a texture which works well to depict "water", and you did a very good job keeping the texture of the ice cream.  Hopefully, you got to eat the evidence after the picture was taken.', '2006-07-28 08:00:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2671489, 362916, 43410, '<td valign="top">this is amazing.  GREAT job :)</td>', 'this is amazing.  GREAT job :)', '2006-07-28 14:20:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2671583, 364503, 17851, '<td valign="top">this is really nice and really different! Its very creative because you focused on the tip of the stem instead of the actual cherry making it original. I would like to see it in color just to compare it to the B&amp;W. Good Job ;)</td>', 'this is really nice and really different! Its very creative because you focused on the tip of the stem instead of the actual cherry making it original. I would like to see it in color just to compare it to the B&W. Good Job ;)', '2006-07-28 14:47:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2671874, 364770, 47852, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First Impression:<br/>Very bright and bold colors, almost a bit hard to look at.  I like the swirls of reds and how all the colors seem to mix into each other.  The kiwi is a great focal point with all the little black seeds.  I like that it is abstract yet you still know what you''re looking at.<br/> <br/>Composition/Background:<br/>The portrait orientation here just feels a bit awkward to me.  Thinking in the rule of thirds, this one seems to be almost split in half with the kiwi and the red colors, and the kiwi is almost centered in the top.  Perhaps a slightly different crop would help?<br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>The one thing that stand out to me technically is the focus.  I like how the focus on the kiwi and bubbles is sharp, yet the rest of the photo is very soft.  <br/> <br/>Post Processing:<br/>You didn''t mention any of your post processing in your photographers notes which makes it difficult to comment on what was done.  It looks as though the saturation was boosted, and the yellows are a bit overdone for my taste.  There are also a few little dark spots of red that I might have cloned out if possible.<br/> <br/>Hope you found this critique helpful!  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First Impression:Very bright and bold colors, almost a bit hard to look at.  I like the swirls of reds and how all the colors seem to mix into each other.  The kiwi is a great focal point with all the little black seeds.  I like that it is abstract yet you still know what you''re looking at. Composition/Background:The portrait orientation here just feels a bit awkward to me.  Thinking in the rule of thirds, this one seems to be almost split in half with the kiwi and the red colors, and the kiwi is almost centered in the top.  Perhaps a slightly different crop would help? Technicals:The one thing that stand out to me technically is the focus.  I like how the focus on the kiwi and bubbles is sharp, yet the rest of the photo is very soft.   Post Processing:You didn''t mention any of your post processing in your photographers notes which makes it difficult to comment on what was done.  It looks as though the saturation was boosted, and the yellows are a bit overdone for my taste.  There are also a few little dark spots of red that I might have cloned out if possible. Hope you found this critique helpful!  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions.', '2006-07-28 16:32:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672009, 364497, 17851, '<td valign="top">Great colors and texture! congrats on the blue!</td>', 'Great colors and texture! congrats on the blue!', '2006-07-28 17:26:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672011, 364733, 17851, '<td valign="top">great job! congrats on ANOTHER ribbon ;)</td>', 'great job! congrats on ANOTHER ribbon ;)', '2006-07-28 17:27:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672012, 362916, 17851, '<td valign="top">congrats on 3rd!! great macro :)</td>', 'congrats on 3rd!! great macro :)', '2006-07-28 17:27:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672048, 364503, 40679, '<td valign="top">I love shallow DoF, and this looks amazing! focus is spot on, composition looks great.<br/>I do wonder why you used b&amp;w for this photo, I think the reddish color of the cherry could also be very nice in the "background"</td>', 'I love shallow DoF, and this looks amazing! focus is spot on, composition looks great.I do wonder why you used b&w for this photo, I think the reddish color of the cherry could also be very nice in the "background"', '2006-07-28 17:39:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672121, 364105, 52713, '<td valign="top">---Greetings from the Critique Club!---<br/> <br/>First impression - Neat idea with the DNA!<br/> <br/>This shot is a good idea that could have used some more pre-shot prep. With the totally white background there is no context. I don''t have any specific suggestions for the background, I just think it would have been better with one, although more difficult for sure. <br/> <br/>I would also suggest making the ketchup more red. This challenge used the Advance Editing rules. You could have done a lot to make the ketchup redder. When I first saw the image I though the ketchup was actually pretzels. <br/> <br/>Keep thinking up these clever ideas!<br/> <br/>I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact if you have and question!<br/> <br/>David<br/></td>', '---Greetings from the Critique Club!--- First impression - Neat idea with the DNA! This shot is a good idea that could have used some more pre-shot prep. With the totally white background there is no context. I don''t have any specific suggestions for the background, I just think it would have been better with one, although more difficult for sure.  I would also suggest making the ketchup more red. This challenge used the Advance Editing rules. You could have done a lot to make the ketchup redder. When I first saw the image I though the ketchup was actually pretzels.  Keep thinking up these clever ideas! I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact if you have and question! David', '2006-07-28 18:06:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672143, 364733, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greeting from the critique club. Geeze as many ribbons as you have you still want a critique? You should be doing these not asking for them. I''m really not sure what I can do to help you better this shot. Nice focus, nice dof use, excellent lighting as well. COngrats on the Ribbon.</td>', 'Greeting from the critique club. Geeze as many ribbons as you have you still want a critique? You should be doing these not asking for them. I''m really not sure what I can do to help you better this shot. Nice focus, nice dof use, excellent lighting as well. COngrats on the Ribbon.', '2006-07-28 18:13:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672150, 364919, 52713, '<td valign="top">---Greetings from the Critique Club!---<br/> <br/>First Impression - one of the very few true abstracts in the challenge.<br/> <br/>I''ll start by saying that not many of the entries are what I would call true abstracts. This shot is for sure.<br/> <br/>The back lighting works well here. There''s a real nice glow to the whole image. Even though your comments say you used noise reduction I still see quite a bit of noise, especially in the shadows.<br/> <br/>The liquid feel gives a real sense of motion that is hard to capture. This shot has a lot going for it. The voters may have been too hung up on trying to figure out what it is instead of enjoying the sensory treat this image gives.<br/> <br/>I think this shot was under rated, but that''s life at DPC, right?<br/> <br/>I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions!<br/> <br/>David<br/> <br/></td>', '---Greetings from the Critique Club!--- First Impression - one of the very few true abstracts in the challenge. I''ll start by saying that not many of the entries are what I would call true abstracts. This shot is for sure. The back lighting works well here. There''s a real nice glow to the whole image. Even though your comments say you used noise reduction I still see quite a bit of noise, especially in the shadows. The liquid feel gives a real sense of motion that is hard to capture. This shot has a lot going for it. The voters may have been too hung up on trying to figure out what it is instead of enjoying the sensory treat this image gives. I think this shot was under rated, but that''s life at DPC, right? I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions! David ', '2006-07-28 18:15:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672177, 363154, 52713, '<td valign="top">---Greetings from the Critique Club!---<br/> <br/>First impression - not really an abstract<br/> <br/>I think the main lesson here is the fact that real food rarely photographs well. Most of the food art you see in ads and on menus are not real food. Never trust an Ice Cream ad!<br/> <br/>IMO there are many things that contributed to the low score.<br/> <br/>1. The fish is not in focus or just is not sharp<br/>2. It''s not very abstract, this looks just like tuna on rice and some peas, and that is exactly what it is. In your notes you mention bold reds and muted colors of the rice. The reds are not bold and the rice is not muted.<br/>3. This probably wouldn''t score well in a Food challenge either. Not enough contrast, rice looks too oily, tuna looks dirty.<br/> <br/>I''ve seen your work before, very strong. I am sure I am not telling you anything you don''t already know.<br/> <br/>I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions.<br/></td>', '---Greetings from the Critique Club!--- First impression - not really an abstract I think the main lesson here is the fact that real food rarely photographs well. Most of the food art you see in ads and on menus are not real food. Never trust an Ice Cream ad! IMO there are many things that contributed to the low score. 1. The fish is not in focus or just is not sharp2. It''s not very abstract, this looks just like tuna on rice and some peas, and that is exactly what it is. In your notes you mention bold reds and muted colors of the rice. The reds are not bold and the rice is not muted.3. This probably wouldn''t score well in a Food challenge either. Not enough contrast, rice looks too oily, tuna looks dirty. I''ve seen your work before, very strong. I am sure I am not telling you anything you don''t already know. I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions.', '2006-07-28 18:25:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672206, 364541, 52713, '<td valign="top">---Greetings from the Critique Club!---<br/> <br/>First impression - love the color of the mushroom against the dark background and water.<br/> <br/>I agree with you that this isn''t really an abstract. That doesn''t seem to have hurt many of the entries. Still it is an awesome capture. The lighting gives great modeling on the mushroom and glistens off the water nicely. The water framing the subject works really well. The out of focus highlights in the water in the foreground are a little distracting but not much.<br/> <br/>The composition is perfect. the eye hits the mushroom and ten follow the water around the image. Well done, as evidenced by the score from the voters.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on a job well done!<br/> <br/>I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions.<br/> <br/>David<br/></td>', '---Greetings from the Critique Club!--- First impression - love the color of the mushroom against the dark background and water. I agree with you that this isn''t really an abstract. That doesn''t seem to have hurt many of the entries. Still it is an awesome capture. The lighting gives great modeling on the mushroom and glistens off the water nicely. The water framing the subject works really well. The out of focus highlights in the water in the foreground are a little distracting but not much. The composition is perfect. the eye hits the mushroom and ten follow the water around the image. Well done, as evidenced by the score from the voters. Congratulations on a job well done! I hope this was helpful. Feel free to contact me if you have any questions. David', '2006-07-28 18:36:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672442, 364497, 1531, '<td valign="top">Amazing, feels like it''s coming out of my monitor</td>', 'Amazing, feels like it''s coming out of my monitor', '2006-07-28 20:05:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672487, 362916, 23458, '<td valign="top">Initially seeing this in the thumbnail it''s hard to see how it meets the challenge. But on viewing the full size image the shot''s abstract qualities do become apparent. The focus and lighting are spot on. While perhaps not my favourite in the challenge, this is, in my opinion, the best of the three ribbon winners by quite a ways. Congratulations on a great effort.</td>', 'Initially seeing this in the thumbnail it''s hard to see how it meets the challenge. But on viewing the full size image the shot''s abstract qualities do become apparent. The focus and lighting are spot on. While perhaps not my favourite in the challenge, this is, in my opinion, the best of the three ribbon winners by quite a ways. Congratulations on a great effort.', '2006-07-28 20:25:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672517, 364497, 27482, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the win, only ribbon winner in this challenge that I felt really met the challenge head on although I wouldn´t have voted the other two down for it, for me abstract means "not recognizable right away" and the other two it´s obviously a mushroom and a kiwi but here I don´t have a clue what I am looking at.</td>', 'Congrats on the win, only ribbon winner in this challenge that I felt really met the challenge head on although I wouldn´t have voted the other two down for it, for me abstract means "not recognizable right away" and the other two it´s obviously a mushroom and a kiwi but here I don´t have a clue what I am looking at.', '2006-07-28 20:36:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672520, 364733, 27482, '<td valign="top">Yayses!  Stop winning those darn ribbons dude, do I have to come over there and break your right index finger so you can´t take photos anymore?  This is getting annoying, trying to catch up and you always staying ahead of the game, hehe :)  Congrats dude!</td>', 'Yayses!  Stop winning those darn ribbons dude, do I have to come over there and break your right index finger so you can´t take photos anymore?  This is getting annoying, trying to catch up and you always staying ahead of the game, hehe :)  Congrats dude!', '2006-07-28 20:38:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672522, 362916, 27482, '<td valign="top">Congrats dude, really dig the DOF in this one.  Now go out there and get yourself a blue one mate, enough of the red and yellow one´s already :)</td>', 'Congrats dude, really dig the DOF in this one.  Now go out there and get yourself a blue one mate, enough of the red and yellow one´s already :)', '2006-07-28 20:39:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672719, 364695, 55838, '<td valign="top">Oh bummer man!  So sorry to see this.  I love this creative shot.  Still a blue to me.  I would have done the same thing (of course my shot would not have been so cool in the first place!) never guessing that it might get DQ''d.  I guess I''ll file this away to be recalled every time I hit the clone button....kind of scary.</td>', 'Oh bummer man!  So sorry to see this.  I love this creative shot.  Still a blue to me.  I would have done the same thing (of course my shot would not have been so cool in the first place!) never guessing that it might get DQ''d.  I guess I''ll file this away to be recalled every time I hit the clone button....kind of scary.', '2006-07-28 22:16:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672890, 364009, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>This shot makes a great first impression!  The rich colors and lighting give this photo the pop it needs to grab a viewer''s attention quickly.  Also, the dimensions of this shot are not typical, which also helps it stand out from the crowd.<br/> <br/>The only thing I can be critical about is how well it meets the challenge.  This is a great photo both technically and artistically, but with regards to the challenge, it falls short.  However, judging by your score, a lot of the voters forgave this.  This is definitely a shot you should be proud of.</td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  This shot makes a great first impression!  The rich colors and lighting give this photo the pop it needs to grab a viewer''s attention quickly.  Also, the dimensions of this shot are not typical, which also helps it stand out from the crowd. The only thing I can be critical about is how well it meets the challenge.  This is a great photo both technically and artistically, but with regards to the challenge, it falls short.  However, judging by your score, a lot of the voters forgave this.  This is definitely a shot you should be proud of.', '2006-07-28 23:26:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2672936, 364503, 8759, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your nice comments. I used BW cause the coloured one showed not very aesteticaly spots on the cherry. It was the only one left and wasn''t that pretty. BW covered it.</td>', 'Thanks for your nice comments. I used BW cause the coloured one showed not very aesteticaly spots on the cherry. It was the only one left and wasn''t that pretty. BW covered it.', '2006-07-28 23:49:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2673016, 362916, 8367, '<td valign="top">Excellent detail and capture. Congratulations!</td>', 'Excellent detail and capture. Congratulations!', '2006-07-29 00:31:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2673682, 364398, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greeting from the critique club. I have looked over your photo and have a few suggestions. First off I do like the dof use here, and the angle for your photo. I would suggest next time possibly coloring the pasta to add a splash of color to the photo. I''d also suggest a change in the background color. Something white or black to help the subject stand out. Pretty good and even lighting all across the photo. Overall well done. Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'Greeting from the critique club. I have looked over your photo and have a few suggestions. First off I do like the dof use here, and the angle for your photo. I would suggest next time possibly coloring the pasta to add a splash of color to the photo. I''d also suggest a change in the background color. Something white or black to help the subject stand out. Pretty good and even lighting all across the photo. Overall well done. Good luck in future challenges.', '2006-07-29 10:45:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2673702, 364742, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club. After looking over your photo I have some comments I''d like to share. First let me say that I love the colors of the photo. Great job of picking your subject and their colors. Nice choice of using natural lighting to light the subject. I like the angle at which you chose to shoot it at. I''m not too sure I like the crop of the photo would like to see a taller vertical crop, it may help the look or hurt, hard to say without seeing. Just an idea. I''d also like to see the foreground in the lower right a bit more in focus. It seems a bit soft. Add a little contrast and some saturation to help with the "pop" factor and I think you add more to your even impressive score. Nicely done overall fit the challenge very well.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club. After looking over your photo I have some comments I''d like to share. First let me say that I love the colors of the photo. Great job of picking your subject and their colors. Nice choice of using natural lighting to light the subject. I like the angle at which you chose to shoot it at. I''m not too sure I like the crop of the photo would like to see a taller vertical crop, it may help the look or hurt, hard to say without seeing. Just an idea. I''d also like to see the foreground in the lower right a bit more in focus. It seems a bit soft. Add a little contrast and some saturation to help with the "pop" factor and I think you add more to your even impressive score. Nicely done overall fit the challenge very well.', '2006-07-29 10:59:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2674208, 364733, 50231, '<td valign="top">Gave you a 9. What else can I say you are a machine!  :-)<br/> <br/>Congrats Man! Another of many fine images!</td>', 'Gave you a 9. What else can I say you are a machine!  :-) Congrats Man! Another of many fine images!', '2006-07-29 15:41:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2674446, 364833, 62755, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by theSaj:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nicely composed and layed out. What was the background? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not sure... but it looks like blue blinds to me... Nice pic btw.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-29 16:41:59.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by theSaj: Very nicely composed and layed out. What was the background?   Not sure... but it looks like blue blinds to me... Nice pic btw.', '2006-07-29 17:41:46.000000', '2006-07-29 17:41:59.000000', 0),
