(2675197, 364763, 21816, '<td valign="top"><b>* Greetings from the Critique Club*</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Ben. First up, congratulations on your highest scoring image. I''ve always preferred the ''less is more'' style of photograph and this is a classic example. You obviously put in a lot of effort to get this one.<br/> <br/>The colours are striking and you resisted from the ''too much saturation'' syndrome which can happen with images like this. I find the blacks of the seeds and around the strawberry seem a little strange looking, almost painted on. It could be from the PP perhaps.<br/> <br/>Your framing and focus are good. I''ve been sitting here trying to look at your lighting as the shadow looks a bit wierd in that it seems ''cut off'' on the edge. I could be just being picky here though.<br/> <br/>All up, it''s a great simple photo and it was received very well. Good stuff. Best of luck in your future challenges.<br/> <br/>Neil</td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club*  Hi Ben. First up, congratulations on your highest scoring image. I''ve always preferred the ''less is more'' style of photograph and this is a classic example. You obviously put in a lot of effort to get this one. The colours are striking and you resisted from the ''too much saturation'' syndrome which can happen with images like this. I find the blacks of the seeds and around the strawberry seem a little strange looking, almost painted on. It could be from the PP perhaps. Your framing and focus are good. I''ve been sitting here trying to look at your lighting as the shadow looks a bit wierd in that it seems ''cut off'' on the edge. I could be just being picky here though. All up, it''s a great simple photo and it was received very well. Good stuff. Best of luck in your future challenges. Neil', '2006-07-30 00:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
